Z||000011||William Federle||11-17-2001||06:19 PM||||I just read a similar story on the technet, except that the writer had found the culprit. It was a wire to the EGR solenoid that was shorted to the block. It had blown the fuse feeding it. The same fuse also feeds one bank of injectors. (It was a V6)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||11-17-2001||06:27 PM||||lol<BR>*knocks MaryJane's, Sloth's, and Ice's heads together*<BR>Smartarsses  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I started noticing this problem AFTER I had the cat cut off. The day I had the Cat removed, I could feel the loss of bottom end, but much nicer top... The problem started about 2 weeks after...<P>I'm leaning towards coil, myself... When the weather was hot, I was starting to see some heat-stress problems. Hot-wired my fan to keep things cool, and that abated.. I MIGHT have a weak spark... <BR>Can't explain why it runs so nice after an ECM reset, though... Unless the timing tables change, too?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>I'll save some pennies and re-work my ignition system.<P>I'll also tear-down and clean up my EGR system. The damn thing IS starting to act up, I think...<P>Any other theories? ||||reg||10
